 "result": "All of this is in `src/tessel/views.py`.\n\n**Conversion to a view function:** `View.to_view_func(name, *class_args, **class_kwargs)` (L86) builds a closure `view(**kwargs)`.\n- By default it creates a new instance of the class on every request and calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`. If `init_every_request = False`, it shares one instance instead.\n- It applies any `cls.decorators`, then attaches `view_class`, `__name__`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` to the function.\n- The function is registered with `app.attach_route_rule(path, view_func=...)`.\n\n**Method set:** `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (L165) sets `cls.methods` automatically. It combines the base classes' `methods` with an upper-cased entry for each name in `http_method_funcs` that the class defines (`get`, `post`, and so on). The route is then registered for exactly those HTTP methods.\n\n**Per-request routing:** `VerbView.run_view` (L182) looks up `getattr(self, request.method.lower())` and calls it with the URL kwargs through `ensure_sync`.\n- If the request is `HEAD` and there is no `head` method, it falls back to `get`.\n- If no handler exists, the assertion fails with \"Unimplemented method\".\n\n`View` itself is the base class. Its `run_view` isn't implemented, so you subclass it or use `VerbView`.",
